  "text": "Global warming is the long -term rise in Earth's average surface temperature caused mainly by human activities that increase greenhouse gases in the atmosphere. Burying fossil fuels for electricity, transportation, and industry releases carbon dioxide, methane, and nitrous oxide, which trap heat that would otherwise escape into space. Deforestation reduces the planet's ability to absorb carbon dioxide because trees act as natural carbon sinks while also releasing stored carbon when they're cut or burned. As the atmosphere warms, ice sheets and glaciers melt, contributing to sea level rise and altering ocean currents that regulate climate patterns. Warmer oceans hold less dissolved oxygen. Harming Marine Eco -",
